WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:17.497
It was a dark, starless night. The moon was hidden in the cloudy sky.

2
00:00:17.498 --> 00:00:22.618
Peter crawled on his belly, snake-like, across the ground.

3
00:00:22.619 --> 00:00:26.816
This was one of many useful things the Indians had taught him.

4
00:00:26.817 --> 00:00:34.614
Tinker Bell was still too weak to fly and light the way, so Peter had decided not to fly himself.

5
00:00:34.615 --> 00:00:40.020
He knew where he was headed—the pirate ship, the Jolly Roger!

6
00:00:40.021 --> 00:00:46.213
Suddenly, Peter caught sight of the crocodile, which was also creeping in the dark.

7
00:00:46.214 --> 00:00:51.628
No other living creature seemed to be awake but the boy and the crocodile.

8
00:00:51.629 --> 00:00:56.934
And they were both after the same prey—Captain Hook.

9
00:00:56.935 --> 00:01:02.916
In the silence of the night, Peter realized something was different about the crocodile.

10
00:01:02.917 --> 00:01:06.690
The clock inside it had finally stopped ticking.

11
00:01:06.691 --> 00:01:10.453
At that moment, Peter had an idea.

12
00:01:10.454 --> 00:01:17.785
He was determined to rescue Wendy and the boys, but he was also eager to destroy his rival.

13
00:01:17.786 --> 00:01:23.785
"This time, it's Hook or me!" he thought with great excitement.

14
00:01:23.786 --> 00:01:26.669
And he started to form a plan.

15
00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:31.589
The Jolly Roger was anchored not far from the shore of Kidd's Creek.

16
00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:38.809
On board, some of the pirates were sleeping, and others were playing dice and cards.

17
00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:47.179
Even though it was after midnight, Smee sat at the ship's sewing machine, busily mending the captain's clothes.

18
00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:50.765
Hook walked the deck deep in thought.

19
00:01:50.766 --> 00:01:55.481
This should have been his moment of triumph. Peter was dead.

20
00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:59.056
The boys were tied up and soon would walk the plank.

21
00:01:59.057 --> 00:02:04.712
And Wendy was his captive. But Hook felt unhappy and alone.

22
00:02:04.713 --> 00:02:08.490
Even among his pirates, Hook was lonely.

23
00:02:08.491 --> 00:02:12.059
They were no better than dogs that obeyed him.

24
00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:16.714
They certainly were not equals who could listen to his feelings.

25
00:02:16.715 --> 00:02:24.404
How cruel fate had been to the captain! Hook hadn't always been a pirate.

26
00:02:24.405 --> 00:02:27.056
Hook wasn't even his real name.

27
00:02:27.057 --> 00:02:31.612
Once, he had been a promising young man at a private school.

28
00:02:31.613 --> 00:02:37.388
There he had learned the manners and fancy dress that could have made him a gentleman.

29
00:02:37.389 --> 00:02:42.777
But he had wanted fame, and evil had taken hold of him.

30
00:02:42.778 --> 00:02:46.025
"What good are all my evil triumphs in the end?

31
00:02:46.026 --> 00:02:49.957
No little children love me," he thought.

32
00:02:49.958 --> 00:02:53.729
It was strange that he should suddenly think of these things.

33
00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:58.148
Maybe it was the sound of Smee's sewing machine.

34
00:02:58.149 --> 00:03:02.610
Even though he was a pirate, old Smee was lovable.

35
00:03:02.611 --> 00:03:07.590
There was not a child on board the ship who did not already love Smee.

36
00:03:07.591 --> 00:03:17.837
He had given Wendy a cloak to keep warm, and Michael had even tried on his glasses.

37
00:03:17.838 --> 00:03:22.359
"What does Smee have that I do not?" wondered Hook.

38
00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:26.484
He needed to do something wicked to feel better again.

39
00:03:26.485 --> 00:03:34.898
Standing a little taller, Hook shouted to his men, "Are all the boys chained so they cannot fly away?"

40
00:03:34.899 --> 00:03:38.545
"Ay, ay," they answered.

41
00:03:38.546 --> 00:03:42.270
"Then bring them up," he ordered.

42
00:03:42.271 --> 00:03:46.151
The poor prisoners were dragged from the hold below.

43
00:03:46.152 --> 00:03:49.711
The eight boys stood in a line in front of him.

44
00:03:49.712 --> 00:03:52.594
"Six of you will walk the plank tonight.

45
00:03:52.595 --> 00:03:59.689
But I will keep two to be my cabin boys. Who wishes to serve me?"

46
00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:05.015
The boys were silent. Finally Tootles spoke up.

47
00:04:05.016 --> 00:04:10.140
"Sir, I don't think my mother would like me to be a pirate.

48
00:04:10.141 --> 00:04:14.152
Would your mother like you to be a pirate, Slightly?"

49
00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:24.310
"I don't think so," Slightly answered sadly, as if he wished it were otherwise. The other boys agreed.

50
00:04:24.311 --> 00:04:29.021
Hook was angry. He looked directly at John.

51
00:04:29.022 --> 00:04:33.861
"You seem to have a little more courage, boy," he said.

52
00:04:33.862 --> 00:04:36.623
"Did you ever want to be a pirate?"

53
00:04:36.624 --> 00:04:43.242
John became thoughtful. "Yes, there was a time when I wanted to be a pirate."

54
00:04:43.243 --> 00:04:48.973
Then he looked around at his friends. "But that was long ago."

55
00:04:48.974 --> 00:04:53.189
"Then go to your doom!" Hook roared.

56
00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:57.252
To his men he said, "Get the plank ready!

57
00:04:57.253 --> 00:05:05.793
And bring up their mother to watch!"
